title crypto — Elligator 2 over Curve25519, Rye-native, GREEN
prompt Read REMEMBER + the 1024-round itinerary, six-season, and Rye-first-crypto wave; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Rye prioritized, send often, stop at the custody gates.
think Walked REMEMBER (living edge was the SIXTEENTH Monocypher-source parity rung, HKDF-SHA-512) and the three design docs. Season G — Cryptography is the open double-seat crux: reimplement Monocypher primitives in Rye with byte-for-byte parity, audit-ready. Confirmed the custody gates (a key, a signature with the maintainer identity, provisioning, paying, the seed force-push) and that this work is gate-free.
think Surveyed the Monocypher API surface against the sixteen landed rungs. Every high-Lindy primitive with a Rye module (BLAKE2b keyed/var, X25519 public, Ed25519 keypair, edx both directions, the ChaCha/Poly line, SHA-512/HMAC/HKDF, verify) is already parity-proven. The genuine remaining primitives with NO Rye yet: Elligator 2 (map/rev/key_pair), x25519_inverse, x25519_dirty_fast/small, and the streaming contexts. Elligator 2 is the standout — the censorship-resistant handshake primitive (hides an X25519 public key as a uniform random string), local oracle (vendored Monocypher, no network fetch), builds on the GREEN fe25519 base field. Chose it crux-first; SLH-DSA (higher strategic crux) wants vendored FIPS 205 KATs, a provisioning/check-in consideration Keaton already flagged.
think Approved my own design round. De-risked the ALGEBRA first with a big-integer Zig scratch (u1024 modular arithmetic) checked against Monocypher's OWN published elligator_dir + elligator_inv vectors before writing any limb code. Found and fixed one real edge bug: in the map's non-square branch u must be r²·ufactor (the squared representative), not r·ufactor — pairs 1..3 are is_square cases where u is overwritten with 1, hiding the bug; pair 4 is the first non-square case that exposes it. After the fix: all 4 direct KATs pass, both inverse KATs pass byte-exact, round-trip closes for all 40 seeds.
think Derived the three Elligator constants from the field rather than copying Monocypher's own 10-limb basis (clean-room): A = 486662, A² = A·A, ufactor = −2·√(−1). The one embedded value is √(−1); reconstructed Monocypher's sqrtm1 from its 10-limb form and verified it equals the canonical ref10 value (√(−1)² = p−1), so the invsqrt branch picks the SAME representative Monocypher would — the property byte-for-byte parity depends on.
think Authored crypto/elligator.rye over the GREEN crypto/fe25519.rye: added the field helpers fe25519 lacked (neg, constant-time ccopy, is_odd, fe_eq, fe_is_zero, a clean fixed-pattern pow_p58 = x^(2^252−3), and invsqrt returning {isr, is_square}), then map and rev ported line-for-line from the validated algebra. Selftest anchors on the four direct KATs (both branches), the three inverse KATs (an unrepresentable point + two representable under tweak 0/1), the round-trip identity across 48 seeds, and the r=0 edge. GREEN on the first metal pass.
obs Rye-first held: the primitive landed in Rye before any Glow surface, over a green-witnessed field. This lap ADDED a crypto file, so the count guard moved 57 → 58 (thirty-seven primitives + twenty-one compositions); crypto_elligator_witness registered in the suite, count guard GREEN, TAME style bans clean (elligator.rye carries asserts, mirrors fe25519.rye's compound-bound style). Zig ships no Elligator, so unlike the hash/cipher rungs there is no std.crypto oracle — the round-trip identity plus Monocypher's own published vectors are the anchors in-module, and the byte-for-byte Monocypher-SOURCE parity witness is the next round.
obs Docs synced same round (docs-implementation-sync): crypto/README.md gained a "Key hiding (Elligator 2)" row and moved 57 → 58 files / 36 → 37 primitives / suite 55 → 58; docs/CRYPTO.md gained the elligator rung row and moved 35 → 37 primitives / 57 → 58 files / 56 → 58 witnesses (correcting pre-existing count drift where I was already touching the lines).
obs Custody-clean and purely local — no key, no signature, no network, no funds, no real device. The inverse map's one representability test is deliberately variable-time (keys tried at random); constant-time timing-safety stays the Season's named horizon.
